[Music]  okay everybody so this is my  spoiler-free review of season one of  halo so  just to make clear they have only sent  the first two episodes to critics for  halo season one so it's so hard when you  do this because i'm only basing this off  of two episodes but that's what we got  right so that's what i can judge it off  of but i want to say that i am a huge  fan of the halo games i grew up playing  the first three games and i've spent  many hours playing the multiplayer of  halo and i actually prefer local  multiplayer and i've had some of the  best memories playing this game with  friends some of the most joy it's  brought me so i was really excited for  this show i had lower expectations  because i was a little worried about the  trailers i wasn't sure how i felt about  it but it's exciting about stephen  spielberg is an executive producer on  this even though it's from a distance  his creative control he's been trying to  get this made for years it has been in  developmental hell for almost a decade  so it's exciting it actually has  happened now seeing the first two  episodes i gotta say i was pretty  impressed by this now i think without  i'm not going to spoil anything here so  don't worry about that so what i'm going  to say is that  i think that this show actually leans  more towards halo fans that maybe its  weaknesses it's not i don't think gonna  be as appealing as just a regular tv  show to someone who's not a halo fan but  i think  it does right by the halo fans and that  audience and that what keeps me  intrigued is having played the games i  get a little bit of those nerd chills  coming in when i see certain things that  you'll see appear just in the first two  episodes alone now the show looks great  it looks better than it did in the  trailers i was thoroughly impressed by  that and it has some exciting action  sequences but what will get you excited  is that it focuses on character and it  puts value in writing so  that gives me hope for this season right  and i think it was a smart decision the  show runners have said that they want to  make the show its own entity in the halo  universe but not can into the game so  they're keeping it separate so that the  games don't rely on the show and vice  versa which i think was smart and you'll  see that and they're kind of putting  their own twist on the tail of master  chief here which i think really works  and the way they're doing it is angling  for it to work as a tv series which is  smart you know they're not making the  bible the game story which i like and  you'll see pablo schreiber who plays  master chief does a great job already  one of the complaints i do have though  from watching it is he's very  very similar to the mandalorian the  character and how he kind of comes off  with his mask on that's my only critique  and it's not something i can really hold  against the show but the mandalorians  the most popular show in the world so  you know you're not going to help but  notice these things it's very soon so  that's one of my critiques but again  he's great at the role it's just a  little similar you know flies a little  closer to the sun to the mandalorian the  show but again it's not something it's  not a bad idea right to be inspired by a  show that works really well in many ways  and you'll see a lot of star wars  inspiration in the show in general i do  think the premiere is a little stronger  than episode two but you'll see in  episode two there's a lot of mystery  built in and i really don't want to  spoil anything but there's a lot of cool  stuff they're doing and you're kind of  wondering even as a halo fan like okay  where are they going to go with this but  it's intriguing and every character is  getting a character arc there's not  paper thin characters here and even the  villains they're getting motivation and  you're kind of seeing it slowly build  they're giving you little bread crumbs  it's a little slow at parts and you  might zone out a bit at parts but it  sucks you right back in when you start  feeling that again because really good  acting all around too and the characters  that are the side characters here that  are you know they're building to be main  characters they have great chemistry  with master chief and they're all  likable there's no one i'm rolling my  eyes at which i'm relieved by you know  and they're good young actresses here  and young actors and  i see full potential for this to be a  great full season so again when you're  seeing these season one reviews come out  it's only based on the first two  episodes but my overall score for it is  going to be an 8.2  i'm gonna give the premiere an 8.7 and  episode two will bring down to just like  an eight so it kind of i'm gonna bring  this all as a whole to an 8.2 but that's  only based on the first two episodes but  it's exciting stuff i think this show is  going to be a hit with halo fans for  sure and honestly just sci-fi fans it is  very sci-fi but if you're out of that  realm i don't think this show really is  something you'd be interested in but  give it a try but if you like you know  star wars stuff if you like bad star  galactica stuff i think you'll like it  if you like anything based off video  games and of course if you like halo i  think this succeeds i don't think halo  fans are gonna be angry about this i  know i'm not i think this is way better  than i thought and you know what for a  video game tv adaptation where there's  not a lot of good adaptations of video  game anything  this is pretty solid so  it could go either way though this is  the first two episodes so you know i  could see it falling off  midway and coming off the rails or i  could see it getting better so i think  it has  the tools here to be a really good show  and i think from the first two episodes  i'm impressed and it's way better than i  thought it would be so i'm excited to  see what you guys think about it let me  know if you plan on watching it if what  you are expecting to see what you're  excited to see let me know i'll be doing  reviews of it every week so make sure to  subscribe i'm gonna review every single  episode and please follow me at steve  varley show on twitter instagram and  tick tock for more of me and i'll see  you next time

